    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-n/q9-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"From x(x + 2)y′ = y, write x(x + 2) dy = y dx. Clear the partial-fraction denominators: x(x + 2) ≡A 1 B x + x + 2, 1 ≡A(x + 2) + Bx •x = 0 ⇒1 = 2A A = 1 2 •x = −2 ⇒1 = −2B B = −1 2 Separate variables and use partial fractions:  1 dy dx 1  y = x(x + 2) = 2x − dx. [M1] [M1] [A1] 2(x + 2)\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-n/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The source uses the initial point as the lower limit. Doubling both sides before integrating gives Z y Z x 2 1 1  v dv = u − du u + 2 2 2 [2 ln |y|]y y=2 = [ln |x| −ln |x + 2|]x x=2 2 ln |y| −2 ln 2 = (ln |x| −ln |x + 2|) −(ln 2 −ln 4) x + 2| −ln 1 x ln y2 −ln 4 = ln | 2 ln(y2 x 4 ) = ln | x + 2| + ln 2 ln(y2 4 ) = ln | 2x x + 2| y2 2x 4 = x + 2 8x y2 = x + 2\" style=\"--madas-width:498.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-n/q9-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Equivalently, indefinite integration gives 2 ln y = ln(x/(x + 2)) + C, [M1] [A1] so y2 = Kx/(x + 2). [M1] [A1] The given point gives 4 = K/2, [M1] [A1] hence y2 = 8x/(x + 2) . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:674.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 9 is 11 marks.</p>"
    ],
