    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-n/q12",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-n/q12-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A curve C has implicit equation xy x ( − y ) 16 + = 0 ,    x ≠ y ,   , x y ≠ 0 . Find the coordinates of the stationary point of  C . ( ) 9\" style=\"--madas-width:592.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-n/q12-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Differentiate x2y −xy2 + 16 = 0 [M1] [A1] implicitly using the product rule twice: dx(x2y) −d d dx(xy2) = d dx(−16) 2xy + x2 dy dx −y2 −x(2y dy dx) = 0 2xy + x2 dy dx −y2 −2xy dy dx = 0 Collect the derivative terms to obtain (x2 −2xy)dy dx = y2 −2xy. [M1] [A1] Since y̸ = 0, stationarity requires y = 2x. [A1] Substituting into the original equation gives x(2x)[x −2x] + 16 = 0 −2x3 + 16 = 0 16 = 2x3\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
